{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.exists_stress_for_every_einstein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.exists_stress_for_every_einstein","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L360-L366","doc":"The Einstein identity is solvable for **every** choice of Einstein term, so\nit excludes no candidate `G` whatever.  Immediate from\n`einstein_split_iff`, and recorded separately because it is the form the\nanti-laundering rule is usually stated in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.einstein_split_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.einstein_split_iff","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L345-L358","doc":"**What the Einstein identity constrains, exactly.**  `gravity = G + T` says\nprecisely that `T` is the residual `gravity − G`; it says nothing at all\nabout `G`.  So the identity **defines** the stress term once the Einstein\nterm is chosen, and **decomposes** neither — AGENTS.md §\"Defined residual ≠\nderived decomposition\", stated in Lean.\n\nThis is orthogonal to the rank of the objects and is untouched by the\n2026-09-15 retype: it is the reason `hasMonoidalEOM_of_def` can discharge\nall three equations by `rfl`, and it stays open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.exists_contract_not_reflecting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.exists_contract_not_reflecting","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L339-L343","doc":"Contrapositive form: two distinct rank-2 fields that a contraction cannot\ntell apart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.subsingleton_of_contract_reflects","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.subsingleton_of_contract_reflects","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L323-L337","doc":"**The converse fails: a scalar contraction cannot state a rank-2\nidentity.**  If equality of contractions implied equality of the rank-2\nfields, uniformly in the co-pairing, then there would be at most one\npairing `X ⊗ Y ⟶ 𝟙_ C`.\n\nThe invariant is `zero_comp`: the degenerate co-pairing `η = 0` contracts\nevery field to the same scalar, so it separates nothing.  Hence in any\n`Preadditive` monoidal category whose pairing space has two distinct\nelements, the scalar Einstein-shaped equation this module used to carry is\n**strictly weaker** than the rank-2 identity it is named after. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.einstein_contracted_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.einstein_contracted_comp","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L314-L321","doc":"The same bridge with the contraction unfolded, so the recovered statement\nis visibly the old one: an equation in `End(𝟙_C)` between the gravity\nscalar and the sum of the Einstein and stress scalars. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.einstein_contracted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.einstein_contracted","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L302-L312","doc":"**The bridge.**  Contracting the rank-2 Einstein identity against any\nco-pairing `η` yields the scalar equation this module used to state\ndirectly.  The proof rewrites by the rank-2 identity and then uses\nadditivity of `contract` — so the scalar form is recovered, not assumed,\nand the retype is a refactor rather than a replacement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.hasMonoidalEOM_of_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.hasMonoidalEOM_of_def","kind":"instance","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L264-L288","doc":"**Reflexivity-like default**: when the variational data is\n*defined* such that each EOM identity holds by `rfl` (i.e.,\nthe gravity/gauge/matter morphisms are constructed as the\nsums of the corresponding currents), the typeclass is\ninhabited trivially.\n\nConcretely: if `vd.gravity := ec.einsteinTensor + ec.stressTensor`,\n`vd.gauge := ec.gaugeCurrent`, `vd.matter := 0` definitionally,\nthen `HasMonoidalEOM` follows by `rfl`.\n\n**This survived the 2026-09-15 retype unchanged, and that is the honest\nreport**: rank and tautology are independent defects.  A `HasMonoidalEOM`\nobtained this way carries no information about `ec` — see\n`einstein_split_iff` for the exact statement of what the identity does and\ndoes not constrain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM.transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM.transport","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L262-L262","doc":"**Transport**: `matter = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM.yang_mills","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM.yang_mills","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L260-L260","doc":"**Yang-Mills**: `gauge = J_ψ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM.einstein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM.einstein","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L258-L258","doc":"**Einstein**: `gravity = G_λ + T_q`, as pairings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM.mk","kind":"ctor","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L254-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasMonoidalEOM","kind":"class","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L249-L262","doc":"**Categorical equations of motion typeclass**: bundles the\nthree on-shell variational identities.  The Einstein field is now stated\nwhere a rank-2 identity can live. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents.gaugeCurrent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents.gaugeCurrent","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L235-L235","doc":"Gauge current density `J_ψ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents.stressTensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents.stressTensor","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L233-L233","doc":"Stress-energy tensor `T_q` — **rank-2**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents.einsteinTensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents.einsteinTensor","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L231-L231","doc":"Einstein tensor `G_λ` — **rank-2**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents.mk","kind":"ctor","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L228-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.ExternalCurrents","kind":"structure","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L223-L235","doc":"**External-current data** — sources for the equations of motion.\nEinstein tensor, stress-energy, gauge current.\n\nThe Einstein and stress terms are **rank-2**; the gauge current is a scalar,\nunchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData.matter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData.matter","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L221-L221","doc":"Matter / transport term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData.gauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData.gauge","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L219-L219","doc":"Yang-Mills / gauge term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData.gravity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData.gravity","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L217-L217","doc":"Einstein / gravity term — **rank-2**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L214-L214","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.VariationalData","kind":"structure","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L208-L221","doc":"**Variational data** — three components of a Lagrangian\ndecomposition: gravity, gauge, matter.\n\n`gravity` is rank-2 (a pairing); `gauge` and `matter` are scalars, exactly\nas before.  Only `gravity` moved, because only it is summed against the\nEinstein and stress terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction.ofContraction_action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction.ofContraction_action","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L200-L204","doc":"Definitional unfolding of the existence constructor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction.ofContraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction.ofContraction","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L186-L198","doc":"**Existence constructor.**  Contract a rank-2 field against a co-pairing\n`η`, then read the resulting scalar with `ε`.\n\nThis is what the previous typing could not support.  With domain\n`End(𝟙_C)` the class was declared and never inhabited anywhere in the\ncorpus, and an instance would have had nothing to vary; here the same\nscalar ingredients give an action **on the pairings**, whose variational\nderivative is a bilinear form\n(`QOU.Variational.QuadraticAction.ofFunctional_variation`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction.action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction.action","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L184-L184","doc":"The action functional, on the field space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L181-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.HasAction","kind":"class","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L168-L184","doc":"**Action functional** as a typeclass: a scalar-valued map from the **field\nspace** `PairingSpace C X Y` to a coefficient ring `R`.  Stated abstractly\nso concrete categories supply their own action.\n\nThe domain is the pairings, not `End(𝟙_C)`: an action must be a functional\non the thing that is varied, or it has no variational derivative worth the\nname.  See the module docstring.\n\n**Base ring (§7c).** The action codomain is a generic\n`{R : Type*}` — nothing in this skeleton performs an archimedean\noperation on the action value (no ordering, no `Real.*`), so the\n`ℝ` specialisation would be gratuitous. A concrete instance at a\nreal-analytic category supplies `(R := ℝ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.contract_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.contract_apply","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L160-L162","doc":"Definitional unfolding, recorded for `simp`.  Not a mathematical claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.contract","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.contract","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L149-L158","doc":"**Contraction** of a rank-2 field against a co-pairing\n`η : 𝟙_ C ⟶ X ⊗ Y`, landing in the scalars `End(𝟙_C)` — the slot this\nmodule used to store directly.  Additivity is the content: `map_zero'` and\n`map_add'` are what make this a trace rather than an arbitrary function,\nand they are what lets `einstein_contracted` push a sum through. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.PairingSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar.PairingSpace","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonoidalCalcVar.lean#L138-L143","doc":"**The field space**: the pairings `X ⊗ Y ⟶ 𝟙_ C` on an ordered pair of\nobjects.  A member has two tensor slots, so it is a rank-2 object by its\ntype rather than by its name — which is the whole difference between this\nand `End(𝟙_C)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}